{"name":"Imperial Blue","hex":"#002395","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"imperial","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Related to an empire, emperor, or empress.","Relating to the British imperial system of measurement."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bottle of wine (usually Bordeaux) containing 6 liters of fluid, eight times the volume of a standard bottle.","A writing paper size measuring 30 × 22 inches, or printing paper measuring 32 × 22 inches."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imperial"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Charaxes imperialis","blocks":[{"text":"Charaxes imperialis, the imperial blue charaxes, is a butterfly in the family Nymphalidae. It is found in Guinea-Bissau, Guinea, Sierra Leone, Liberia, Ivory Coast, Ghana, Benin, Nigeria, Cameroon, Equatorial Guinea, the Republic of the Congo, the Central African Republic, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Rwanda, Uganda, Tanzania and Zambia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Charaxes_imperialis.jpg/330px-Charaxes_imperialis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charaxes_imperialis"},{"title":"Jalmenus evagoras","blocks":[{"text":"Jalmenus evagoras, the imperial hairstreak, imperial blue, or common imperial blue, is a small, metallic blue butterfly of the family Lycaenidae. It is commonly found in eastern coastal regions of Australia. This species is notable for its unique mutualism with ants of the genus Iridomyrmex. The ants provide protection for juveniles and cues for adult mating behavior. They are compensated with food secreted from J. evagoras larvae. The ants greatly enhance the survival and reproductive success of the butterflies. J. evagoras lives and feeds on Acacia plants, so butterfly populations are localized to areas with preferred species of both host plants and ants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Common_Imperial_Blue.jpg/330px-Common_Imperial_Blue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalmenus_evagoras"},{"title":"Imperial Blue (whisky)","blocks":[{"text":"Imperial Blue, abbreviated to IB and also known as Seagram's Imperial Blue, is a brand of Indian whisky launched in 1997 and currently owned by Tilaknagar Industries."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/37/Imperial_Blue_logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial_Blue_(whisky)"},{"title":"Royal blue","blocks":[{"text":"Royal blue is a deep and vivid shade of blue. Traditionally, royal blue is a deep shade of blue and is used in several national flags. However, the web color named royal blue is a much brighter shade."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Jalmenus-evagoras-ventral.jpg/500px-Jalmenus-evagoras-ventral.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Jalmenus-evagoras-ventral.jpg/1280px-Jalmenus-evagoras-ventral.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Jalmenus-evagoras-ventral.jpg/500px-Jalmenus-evagoras-ventral.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail"